					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5127</guid>
				<title>The Resurrector</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5127</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP 5127&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP 5127 is to be kept in a glass box in a 4m*2m*3m room made out of titanium and monitored 24/7. If personal tries to resurrect the deceased body for 2nd time they are to be&lt;br /&gt;
stopped before the process of resurrection is completed. If SCP 5127-2 enters the body it is to be incinerated immediately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP 5127 was discovered in Chaco, Argentina in 2003 after civilians were consistently reporting deceased people rising from their graves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP 5127 consists of SCP 5127-1 and SCP 5127-2. SCP 5127-1 is a strangely shaped book with covers made of an unknown harmful white substance and pages are made out of leather. The object appears to have the ability to resurrect deceased people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The process of it resurrecting people consists of users bringing deceased humans within 2 meters to the object and writing the deceased human&#039;s name. People resurrected (now labeled as SCP 5127-3) do not appear to be hostile towards personal and seem to have trouble controlling their body.&lt;br /&gt;
Subjects have full memory of their past. Subjects also seem to be in better condition than they were in before their death. Subjects are more intelligent and stronger.&lt;br /&gt;
The subjects will be alive for a certain time. Time for how long the subject will be alive isn&#039;t determined since some instances of subjects died within&lt;br /&gt;
1 hour while some instances of subjects are still alive years after being resurrected. The subject can be resurrected only once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If the user tries resurrecting&lt;br /&gt;
the same person twice the person trying to be resurrected will become possessed by SCP 5127-2. SCP 5127-2 is a shapeless black entity that comes out of SCP 5127-1 when it&#039;s triggered.&lt;br /&gt;
SCP 5127-2 gets triggered every time the user tries to resurrect the same deceased human twice. After possessing the body the human body will regenerate itself and grow 2 meters taller&lt;br /&gt;
than its original form, the skin will be peeled off and muscle tissues will get black pigment. The possessed body will afterwords roam around the accessible areas slaughtering&lt;br /&gt;
everything in its peripheral vision. SCP 5127-2 possesses incredible strength and resistance to bullets. Once the period between 6-7 hours passes or the possessed body is taken&lt;br /&gt;
down it will leave the deceased person&#039;s body and go back in SCP 5127-1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notes:&lt;/strong&gt; Following the event of ████████ SCP 5127-2 will now attempt to possess bodies that are being resurrected for 1st time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/velja-vraccarevicc&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6524034&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1605860226&quot; alt=&quot;Velja Vraccarevicc&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6524034)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/velja-vraccarevicc&quot;  &gt;Velja Vraccarevicc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
